  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "L-coefficients at x = 3: for x=1: (1)(−1)(−2)/[(−1)(−3)(−4)] = −1/6; for x=2: (2)(−1)(−2)/[(1)(−2)(−3)] = 2/3; for x=4: (2)(1)(−2)/[(3)(2)(−1)] = 2/3; for x=5: (2)(1)(−1)/[(4)(3)(1)] = −1/6. f(3) = −3/6 + 14/3 + 102/3 − 103/6 = 21."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "format": "mcq",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "L-coefficients at x = 3: for x=1: (1)(−1)(−2)/[(−1)(−3)(−4)] = −1/6; for x=2: (2)(−1)(−2)/[(1)(−2)(−3)] = 2/3; for x=4: (2)(1)(−2)/[(3)(2)(−1)] = 2/3; for x=5: (2)(1)(−1)/[(4)(3)(1)] = −1/6. f(3) = −3/6 + 14/3 + 102/3 − 103/6 = 21."
   }
  ]
